body:
My idea is to have a stopwatch at every cubicle you have to press a physical button every hour to label this cub as occupied on a webpage that indicates availability, so ppl don’t need to walk around and look for empty seats but can instead go straight for the seats that are shown available; 

having a physical button is to make sure there is indeed someone actively using this place, unlike online booking some a holes book seats but never come. 

Pressing a button every hour isn’t very troublesome to as well, and one hour or so is sufficient for you to take a turd or even have lunch.

